     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello Geomorph community,</div><div><br></div><div>I have a little question on Repeatability calculation :) </div><div>So, in my dataset are 277 specimens, each one was digitized twice (which means replicates=2). I want to compute repeatability value. Firstly, I read guide from Dr. Sherratt and then this disscusion in geomorph google group (<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/m/#!topic/geomorph-r-package/Cj_CfXzJtrw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/m/%23!topic/geomorph-r-package/Cj_CfXzJtrw&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484532281000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ZGvAWJZD6Kczpw5XkfWNV\">https://groups.google.com/forum/m/#!topic/geomorph-r-package/Cj_CfXzJtrw</a>).</div><div>I did a nested ANOVA:</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><b>id</b>=gl(2,277)          </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">geomorphdataframe=geomorph.data.frame(Shape=Shape,</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">+                                       <b>ind=id,</b></font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">+                                      </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"> </span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">indiv=Specimen_info$individual_names</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">+                                    </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">  </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"></span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">rep=as.factor(Specimen_info$rep)</span></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">+ )</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">anv&lt;-procD.lm(Shape ~ <b>ind</b>, data = geomorphdataframe, iter = 999)<br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">summary(anv)</font></div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Analysis of Variance, using Residual Randomization</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Permutation procedure: Randomization of null model residuals </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Number of permutations: 1000 </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Estimation method: Ordinary Least Squares </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Sums of Squares and Cross-products: Type I </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Effect sizes (Z) based on F distributions</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">           Df      SS       MS     Rsq      F      Z Pr(&gt;F)   </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">ind:rep    <b> 1</b> 0.03971 0.039707 0.02564 14.527 4.4738  0.001 **</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Residuals <b>552</b> 1.50879 0.002733 0.97436                        </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Total     <b>553 </b>1.54850                                         </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">---</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Signif. codes:  0 ‘***’ 0.001 ‘**’ 0.01 ‘*’ 0.05 ‘.’ 0.1 ‘ ’ 1</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Call: procD.lm(f1 = Shape ~ ind:rep, data = geomorphdataframe)</font></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>So, my Repeatability in this case is:</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">(MS(ind:rep) - MS(residuals)) / (MS(ind:rep) + MS(residuals))</font></div><div><br></div><div>Can someone tell me if the formula is <b>correct</b> on <b>not</b>? :)</div><div><br></div><div>Then I was surprised that all individuals are in resudials, so I decided to make procD.lm in a little different way:</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">geomorphdataframe=geomorph.data.frame(Shape=Shape,</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">+                                       ind=id,</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">+                                      </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"> </span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><b>indiv=Specimen_info$individual_names</b></font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">+                                    </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">  </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"></span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">rep=as.factor(Specimen_info$rep)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">+ )</span></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">anv_indiv&lt;-procD.lm(Shape ~ <b>indiv</b>, data = geomorphdataframe, iter = 999)</font><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">summary(anv_indiv)<br></font></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Analysis of Variance, using Residual Randomization</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Permutation procedure: Randomization of null model residuals </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Number of permutations: 1000 </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Estimation method: Ordinary Least Squares </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Sums of Squares and Cross-products: Type I </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Effect sizes (Z) based on F distributions</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">           Df     SS        MS     Rsq      F      Z Pr(&gt;F)   </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">indiv     <b>276</b> 1.3804 0.0050015 0.89144 8.2415 22.969  0.001 **</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Residuals <b>277</b> 0.1681 0.0006069 0.10856                        </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Total     <b>553</b> 1.5485                                          </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">---</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Signif. codes:  0 ‘***’ 0.001 ‘**’ 0.01 ‘*’ 0.05 ‘.’ 0.1 ‘ ’ 1</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Call: procD.lm(f1 = Shape ~ indiv, iter = 999, data = geomorphdataframe)</font></div></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><div>So, my Repeatability in this case is:</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">(MS(indiv) - MS(residuals)) / (MS(indiv) + MS(residuals))</font></div></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><br></div><div>Can someone explaine to me which one <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">procD.lm </font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">formula</font> is correct?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you in advance!</div><div>Lyna</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
