     1,
     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div>\r\n    <p>You could also consult this very interesting discussion on the\r\n      subject previously provided by Mike to another user with the same\r\n      question:</p>\r\n    <p><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?hl=en-GB#!searchin/geomorph-r-package/measurement$20error%7Csort:date/geomorph-r-package/qDvkHPg_XLM/jm_8JVwwCwAJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?hl%3Den-GB%23!searchin/geomorph-r-package/measurement$20error%257Csort:date/geomorph-r-package/qDvkHPg_XLM/jm_8JVwwCwAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484532294000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2DkNXWkBwBv7bEmJzLG9_v\">https://groups.google.com/forum/?hl=en-GB#!searchin/geomorph-r-package/measurement$20error%7Csort:date/geomorph-r-package/qDvkHPg_XLM/jm_8JVwwCwAJ</a></p>\r\n    <p>Antigoni<br>\r\n    </p></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div>\r\n    <div>On 22/04/2020 15:24, Adams, Dean [EEOB]\r\n      wrote:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    </div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      \r\n      \r\n      \r\n      <div>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Lyna,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">In\r\n            general, assessing repeatability is accomplished using some\r\n            variant of the intraclass correlation; which is a ratio of\r\n            variance among individuals as compared to total variation.\r\n            The simplest model would be:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">R\r\n            = S_a^2 / (S_a^2+S_w^2)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Where\r\n            S_a^2 is the among individual variance and S_w^2 is the\r\n            within individual variance. These values are obtained from\r\n            an ANOVA table where variation is partitioned. Doing this\r\n            properly requires matching the data that one has with the\r\n            model being used. I suggest a careful reading of the primary\r\n            literature to sort that out for your particular case (e.g.,\r\n            Arnqvist and Martensson 1998 is a good place to start).\r\n            <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><br>\r\n            Note that Em’s post is based on the logic espoused in this,\r\n            and related papers. She could speak to your specific\r\n            question.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Best,\r\n            <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><br>\r\n            Dean<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Dr.\r\n            Dean C. Adams<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Director\r\n            of Graduate Education, EEB Program<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Professor<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Department\r\n            of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Iowa\r\n            State University<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><a href=\"https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484532295000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07Pw_2aH6Tz_OiaLvT8_tE\">https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">phone:\r\n            <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">515-294-3834</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">\r\n            <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>\r\n            <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;geomorph-...@googlegroups.com&gt;</a>\r\n            <b>On Behalf Of </b>?????? ??????<br>\r\n            <b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, April 22, 2020 4:36 AM<br>\r\n            <b>To:</b> geomorph R package\r\n            <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;geomorph-...@googlegroups.com&gt;</a><br>\r\n            <b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] Repeatability<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n        <div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hello Geomorph community,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\">I have a little question on\r\n              Repeatability calculation :) <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\">So, in my dataset are 277 specimens,\r\n              each one was digitized twice (which means replicates=2). I\r\n              want to compute repeatability value. Firstly, I read guide\r\n              from Dr. Sherratt and then this disscusion in geomorph\r\n              google group (<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/m/#!topic/geomorph-r-package/Cj_CfXzJtrw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/m/%23!topic/geomorph-r-package/Cj_CfXzJtrw&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484532295000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1qpogCiKa96t3quU4Fn1sj\">https://groups.google.com/forum/m/#!topic/geomorph-r-package/Cj_CfXzJtrw</a>).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\">I did a nested ANOVA:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">id</span></b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">=gl(2,277)  \r\n                       </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>geomorphdataframe=geomorph.data.frame(Shape=Shape,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>+                                      \r\n                <b>ind=id,</b></span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>+                                    \r\n                  indiv=Specimen_info$individual_names</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>+                                     \r\n                 rep=as.factor(Specimen_info$rep)</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>+ )</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>anv&lt;-procD.lm(Shape ~\r\n                <b>ind</b>, data = geomorphdataframe, iter = 999)</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>summary(anv)</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Analysis of Variance, using Residual\r\n                Randomization</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Permutation procedure: Randomization of null\r\n                model residuals </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Number of permutations: 1000 </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Estimation method: Ordinary Least Squares </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Sums of Squares and Cross-products: Type I </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Effect sizes (Z) based on F distributions</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>           Df      SS       MS     Rsq      F\r\n                     Z Pr(&gt;F)   </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>ind:rep    <b> 1</b> 0.03971 0.039707 0.02564\r\n                14.527 4.4738  0.001 **</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Residuals <b>552</b> 1.50879 0.002733\r\n                0.97436                        </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Total     <b>553 </b>\r\n                1.54850                                         </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>---</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Signif. codes:  0 ‘***’ 0.001 ‘**’ 0.01 ‘*’\r\n                0.05 ‘.’ 0.1 ‘ ’ 1</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Call: procD.lm(f1 = Shape ~ ind:rep, data =\r\n                geomorphdataframe)</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\">So, my Repeatability in this case is:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>(MS(ind:rep) - MS(residuals)) / (MS(ind:rep)\r\n                + MS(residuals))</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Can someone tell me if the formula is <b>correct</b>\r\n              on <b>not</b>? :)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Then I was surprised that all\r\n              individuals are in resudials, so I decided to make\r\n              procD.lm in a little different way:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>geomorphdataframe=geomorph.data.frame(Shape=Shape,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>+                                      \r\n                ind=id,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>+                                       <b>indiv=Specimen_info$individual_names</b></span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>+                                  \r\n                    rep=as.factor(Specimen_info$rep)</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>+ )</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>anv_indiv&lt;-procD.lm(Shape ~\r\n                <b>indiv</b>, data = geomorphdataframe, iter = 999)</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>summary(anv_indiv)</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Analysis\r\n                  of Variance, using Residual Randomization</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Permutation\r\n                  procedure: Randomization of null model residuals </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Number of\r\n                  permutations: 1000 </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Estimation\r\n                  method: Ordinary Least Squares </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Sums of\r\n                  Squares and Cross-products: Type I </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Effect\r\n                  sizes (Z) based on F distributions</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">         \r\n                   Df     SS        MS     Rsq      F      Z Pr(&gt;F)\r\n                    </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">indiv    \r\n                  <b>276</b> 1.3804 0.0050015 0.89144 8.2415 22.969\r\n                   0.001 **</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Residuals\r\n                  <b>277</b> 0.1681 0.0006069 0.10856                  \r\n                       </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Total    \r\n                  <b>553</b> 1.5485                                    \r\n                       </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">---</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Signif.\r\n                  codes:  0 ‘***’ 0.001 ‘**’ 0.01 ‘*’ 0.05 ‘.’ 0.1 ‘ ’ 1</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Call:\r\n                  procD.lm(f1 = Shape ~ indiv, iter = 999, data =\r\n                  geomorphdataframe)</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\">So, my Repeatability in this case is:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">(MS(indiv)\r\n                  - MS(residuals)) / (MS(indiv) + MS(residuals))</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Can someone explaine to me which one <span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">procD.lm\r\n              </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">formula</span> is\r\n              correct?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thank you in advance!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Lyna<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>\r\n          You received this message because you are subscribed to the\r\n          Google Groups &quot;geomorph R package&quot; group.<br>\r\n          To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from\r\n          it, send an email to\r\n          <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-r-pack...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n          To view this discussion on the web, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/3f6ea8be-fcb2-420d-a44b-e85173391bb8%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/3f6ea8be-fcb2-420d-a44b-e85173391bb8%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484532295000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3uEyF5voC4npdS3ep-cIuG\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/3f6ea8be-fcb2-420d-a44b-e85173391bb8%40googlegroups.com</a>.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n      </div>\r\n      -- <br>\r\n      You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google\r\n      Groups &quot;geomorph R package&quot; group.<br>\r\n      To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it,\r\n      send an email t